-- Traffic Ordinance [New Version], 5721-1961 -- פקודת התעבורה [נוסח חדש]
-- s.64B(a), the definition of "intoxicated" (שיכור), paragraphs (3) and (3A),
-- and s.62(3), the offence of being intoxicated while driving.
-- Traffic Regulations, 5721-1961 -- תקנות התעבורה, התשכ"א-1961
-- reg. 169A, the definition of "alcohol concentration in the body" (ריכוז אלכוהול בגוף).
--
-- WHICH INSTRUMENT CARRIES THE NUMBERS. Two do, and the split is the point.
--   * The GENERAL threshold is not in the Ordinance. s.64B(a)(3) says a person is
--     intoxicated who has alcohol "in a concentration higher than the concentration
--     the Minister prescribed" (בריכוז הגבוה מהריכוז שקבע השר); the Minister
--     prescribed it in reg. 169A of the Traffic Regulations: 240 micrograms of
--     alcohol per litre of exhaled air, or 50 milligrams per 100 millilitres of
--     blood. That definition was inserted by Traffic Regulations (Amendment No. 3)
--     5770-2009, Kovetz HaTakanot 6825 p. 114, published 10 November 2009, which
--     deleted the earlier defined term "המידה הקבועה". What that earlier term said
--     is NOT established here (the 1982 gazette is an image-only scan), so this
--     encoding covers no rules-effective date before 10 November 2009 and says so
--     rather than guessing (NOTES.md, fork F2).
--   * The CLASS-SPECIFIC threshold IS in the Ordinance. Paragraph (3A) of the
--     definition -- 50 micrograms per litre of exhaled air, or 10 milligrams per
--     100 millilitres of blood, for a new driver, a driver under 24, a driver of a
--     commercial or work vehicle over 3,500 kg, and a driver of a public vehicle --
--     was inserted by the Traffic Ordinance Amendment (No. 97) Law 5771-2010,
--     Sefer HaChukim 2265 p. 91, adopted by the Knesset on 29 November 2010 and
--     published 9 December 2010 (both dates from the deposited gazette issue).
--     The Amendment has no commencement clause, so it commenced on publication
--     (NOTES.md, fork F1). Its paragraph (3A) is word for word the paragraph in the
--     consolidated text deposited from Wikisource (2026-09-09 revision).
--
-- THE POINT OF THIS ENCODING is that the threshold lives on L4's rule-effective-time
-- axis: one rule, and `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` picks the vintage. Roznai,
-- "Law 'Wants to be Free'" (HaPraklit 52, 2013), used exactly this amendment: the
-- first Google hit for the Ordinance served a text that omitted Amendment 97, and a
-- reader relying on it would have read the wrong limit for a 22-year-old.
--
-- Not encoded: paragraphs (1) (drinking while driving), (2) (dangerous drugs) and
-- (4) (under the influence, subject to the floor) of the definition; the 3-hour
-- presumption in paragraph (3); the police sampling powers in s.64B(a1)-(o); the
-- "person in charge of the vehicle" limb of s.62(3); and s.12A's derivation of who
-- is a new driver, which is an input here.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- For the ambient case only: `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` with no pin falls back to today,
-- and "today" needs a zone. Every pinned evaluation is independent of this.
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Jerusalem"

§ `The sample, the threshold, the driver`

-- s.64B(a)(3A): "לפי דגימת נשיפה ... או לפי דגימת דם". The units are the statute's:
-- micrograms per litre of exhaled air for breath, milligrams per 100 millilitres for
-- blood. Nothing is converted between them.
DECLARE Sample IS ONE OF
    `breath sample` HAS `micrograms of alcohol per litre of exhaled air` IS A NUMBER
    `blood sample`  HAS `milligrams of alcohol per 100 millilitres of blood` IS A NUMBER

-- Paragraph (4) of the definition calls each pair "the floor" (הסף): the one set by
-- regulations under paragraph (3), and the one stated in paragraph (3A).
DECLARE Threshold HAS
    `micrograms of alcohol per litre of exhaled air`   IS A NUMBER
    `milligrams of alcohol per 100 millilitres of blood` IS A NUMBER

-- s.1 defines "רכב ציבורי" (carries passengers for hire), "רכב מסחרי" (carries goods),
-- "רכב עבודה" (work equipment fitted), "רכב פרטי" (neither public nor commercial).
-- Paragraph (3A)(c) groups the commercial and the work vehicle together and asks
-- one question of both: the permitted gross weight on the vehicle licence.
DECLARE Vehicle IS ONE OF
    `private vehicle`
    `public vehicle`
    `commercial or work vehicle` HAS `permitted gross weight in kilograms` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Driver HAS
    `is a new driver`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- s.12A: two years from the first licence, extendable; an input here
    `age in years`     IS A NUMBER    -- paragraph (3A)(b): "נהג שטרם מלאו לו 24 שנים"
    `vehicle driven`   IS A Vehicle

-- The answer. "שיכור" is the statute's own word; the third value is this encoding's
-- confession that it holds no text for that rules-effective date.
DECLARE Finding IS ONE OF
    `intoxicated`
    `not intoxicated`
    `the text in force on that date is not encoded`

§ `reg. 169A -- the general threshold`

-- "”ריכוז אלכוהול בגוף“ – ריכוז אלכוהול בדגימת אוויר נשוף או בדגימת דם, העולה על אחד
-- מאלה, לפי העניין: (1) 240 מיקרוגרם אלכוהול בליטר אוויר נשוף; (2) 50 מיליגרם אלכוהול
-- במאה מיליליטר דם." -- as inserted 10 November 2009, K.T. 6825 p. 114.
`the general threshold` MEANS
    Threshold WITH `micrograms of alcohol per litre of exhaled air`   IS 240
                   `milligrams of alcohol per 100 millilitres of blood` IS 50

-- The day reg. 169A took its present form. Before it the Regulations defined
-- "המידה הקבועה" instead, in words this encoding has not read (fork F2).
`the earliest rules-effective date this encoding covers` MEANS YMD 2009 11 10

§ `s.64B(a) "intoxicated", paragraph (3A) -- Amendment No. 97`

-- Sefer HaChukim 2265, 2 Tevet 5771 (9 December 2010), p. 91: a one-section Act
-- with no commencement clause. Adopted 22 Kislev 5771 (29 November 2010).
`the commencement of Amendment 97` MEANS YMD 2010 12 9

-- The whole of the versioning is this one line: the rule reads the rule-effective
-- axis, and `EVAL UNDER RULES EFFECTIVE AT` sets it.
`Amendment 97 is in force` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL `the commencement of Amendment 97`

-- "(3א) אחד המנויים להלן שלפי דגימת נשיפה, בגופו מצוי אלכוהול בריכוז העולה על 50
-- מיקרוגרם אלכוהול בליטר אוויר נשוף, או לפי דגימת דם – בריכוז העולה על 10 מיליגרם
-- אלכוהול ב־100 מיליליטר דם:"
`the threshold for the drivers listed in paragraph (3A)` MEANS
    Threshold WITH `micrograms of alcohol per litre of exhaled air`   IS 50
                   `milligrams of alcohol per 100 millilitres of blood` IS 10

-- "(א) נהג חדש; (ב) נהג שטרם מלאו לו 24 שנים; (ג) נהג בעת נהיגה ברכב מסחרי או ברכב
-- עבודה שמשקלם הכולל המותר לפי רישיון הרכב עולה על 3,500 קילוגרם; (ד) נהג בעת נהיגה
-- ברכב ציבורי;"
GIVEN driver IS A Driver
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver is one of those listed in paragraph (3A)` @nlg the driver %driver% is a new driver, is under 24, is driving a commercial or work vehicle over 3,500 kg, or is driving a public vehicle
    IF driver's `is a new driver`
    OR driver's `age in years` LESS THAN 24
    OR CONSIDER driver's `vehicle driven`
       WHEN `public vehicle`                       THEN TRUE
       WHEN `commercial or work vehicle` weight    THEN weight GREATER THAN 3500
       OTHERWISE                                        FALSE

§ `Which threshold, on which day`

-- s.64B(a)(3) sends every driver to the Minister's figure; paragraph (3A), once in
-- force, sends the drivers it lists to its own. NOTHING is the honest answer for a
-- rules-effective date before the Regulations' present text.
GIVEN driver IS A Driver
GIVETH A MAYBE Threshold
DECIDE `the alcohol concentration above which the driver is intoxicated` @nlg the alcohol concentration above which %driver% is intoxicated, under the text in force on the rules-effective date
    IS IF DATE_SERIAL `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the earliest rules-effective date this encoding covers`
       THEN NOTHING
       ELSE IF `Amendment 97 is in force` AND `the driver is one of those listed in paragraph (3A)` driver
            THEN JUST `the threshold for the drivers listed in paragraph (3A)`
            ELSE JUST `the general threshold`

-- "העולה על" -- exceeds. A reading exactly at the figure is not above it.
GIVEN sample    IS A Sample
      threshold IS A Threshold
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sample exceeds the threshold` @nlg the reading in %sample% is higher than the corresponding figure in %threshold%
    IF CONSIDER sample
       WHEN `breath sample` reading THEN reading GREATER THAN threshold's `micrograms of alcohol per litre of exhaled air`
       WHEN `blood sample`  reading THEN reading GREATER THAN threshold's `milligrams of alcohol per 100 millilitres of blood`

@export Whether a driver is "intoxicated" within s.64B(a)(3)-(3A) of the Traffic Ordinance on a given alcohol reading, under the text in force on the rules-effective date
GIVEN driver IS A Driver  @desc the driver: new-driver status (s.12A), age, and the vehicle driven
      sample IS A Sample  @desc the breath or blood reading, in the statute's own units
GIVETH A Finding
DECIDE `the driver is intoxicated` @nlg whether %driver% is intoxicated on %sample%, under the text in force on the rules-effective date
    IS CONSIDER `the alcohol concentration above which the driver is intoxicated` driver
       WHEN NOTHING        THEN `the text in force on that date is not encoded`
       WHEN JUST threshold THEN IF `the sample exceeds the threshold` sample threshold
                                THEN `intoxicated`
                                ELSE `not intoxicated`

§ `s.62(3) -- the offence`

-- "(3) הוא שיכור בהיותו נוהג רכב, או בהיותו ממונה על הרכב, בדרך או במקום ציבורי;
-- לענין זה, ”שיכור“ ו”ממונה על הרכב“ – כהגדרתם בסעיף 64ב;" -- two years'
-- imprisonment or the s.61(a)(3) Penal Law fine. The "person in charge" limb is not
-- encoded.
GIVEN driver IS A Driver
      sample IS A Sample
      `was driving on a road or in a public place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the driver commits the offence under section 62(3)` @nlg whether %driver%, on %sample%, commits the s.62(3) offence of being intoxicated while driving on a road or in a public place
    IS CONSIDER `the driver is intoxicated` driver sample
       WHEN `the text in force on that date is not encoded` THEN NOTHING
       WHEN `intoxicated`     THEN JUST `was driving on a road or in a public place`
       WHEN `not intoxicated` THEN JUST FALSE
